User: icons made by MView could not be opened ("Cannot display this image
saved_previous.ico - Windows can't read this file"), others could.
- Cause: .ico went to WIC only (Batch D); MakeIconFromImage wrote every
  size as PNG through TFPWriterPNG, which drops the alpha channel of an
  opaque picture (CountAlphas: colour type 2). Windows' icon codec reads
  PNG entries only as 32-bit RGBA. The sort panel was not affected (its
  own decoder).
- uIconFile: IconDibEntry (32-bit DIB + AND mask) and IconPngEntry (own
  PNG writer, always RGBA, zstream + crc); WriteIconFile takes entries.
- uMView.MakeIconFromImage: DIB for 16 .. 128 px, RGBA PNG for 256 px;
  FPWritePNG no longer used.
- umedialoader: DecodeIconBitmap (moved from uSortIcons, which now calls
  it) and LoadIcon: an .ico is read by MView first (largest picture),
  WIC only if that fails. Icons made before open again.
- TestSort: TestIconEntries (6 checks; DIB and PNG read back, the PNG by
  FPReadPNG with its alpha): 111 pass. Checked under Wine: the user's
  saved_previous.ico shows (256 x 256).

